#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:1
msgid "Mattermost MCP Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:3
msgid ""
"A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides AI agents and "
"automation tools with secure access to Mattermost channels, users, and "
"content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:5
msgid ""
"**Standalone binary:** The `mattermost-mcp-server` process (for example, "
"stdio transport for local clients) is intended for **development and "
"local tooling only** and is **not** supported for production deployments."
" For production, use the Agents plugin’s embedded MCP and the in-server "
"integration described in the [admin guide](../docs/admin_guide.md"
"#mattermost-mcp-server)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:7
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:9
msgid ""
"**MCP Protocol Support**: Implements the Model Context Protocol for "
"standardized AI agent communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:10
msgid "**Authentication**: Personal Access Token (PAT) authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/mcpserver/README.md:11
msgid ""
"**Transport** (development use): Configurable transport layer (stdio "
"JSON-RPC for desktop clients, HTTP with SSE for web applications). The "
"standalone binary note at the top of this file also applies. For "
"production, use the Agents plugin’s embedded MCP and the [admin "
"guide](../docs/admin_guide.md#mattermost-mcp-server)."
msgstr ""

